{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>Behold, I.</b> HaShem said to Moses that he should also say this to Israel: that if they accept all the words and laws from \"from the beginning you have seen\" onward, then He will bring them into the land. And many have erred in this:" "Some say the angel is the Book of the Torah, because \"My name is within him,\" and others said it is the Ark of the Covenant, and they interpreted \"and heed his voice\" as referring to what is written in it, and they said \"He will not forgive your transgression\" as referring to it. And all these are words of wind, for all of the Torah and Scripture are full of this meaning: \"He will send His angel before you\" (Genesis 24:7), \"The angel who redeems me from all evil\" (Genesis 48:16), and Moses said, \"He sent an angel and brought us out of Egypt\" (Numbers 20:16), and \"the angel of His presence saved them\" (Isaiah 63:9), and \"the angel of YHWH went out\" (Isaiah 37:36), and he said to the destroying angel among the people (II Samuel 24:16), \"My Elohim sent His angel\" (Daniel 6:23), \"like a son of Elohim\" (Daniel 3:25), and many like these, and in the book of Daniel, the prince of Greece and the prince of Persia (Daniel 10), \"for Michael is your prince\" (Daniel 10:21), and he is called \"the great one,\" for he is exalted above many others, and it is written of him, \"one of the chief princes came to help me\" (Daniel 10:13), which means in rank, like \"those who sit first in the kingdom\" (Esther 1:14), and this angel is Michael." "<b>To guard you on the way.</b> That no evil touch you." "<b>Which I have prepared.</b> For you, as in \"When the Most High gave nations their inheritance\" (Deuteronomy 32:8), as I shall explain."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:37:46.146873187Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}